From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:05:30 -0700
Subject: [skia] Update Ganesh flush calls to propagate success

Ganesh's flush now reports success, so update call sites to include that
in their `success` results that were already being propagated up.
Additionaly, raster_decoder's SetCleared() logic is unified now between
Ganesh and Graphite to only mark the shared image as cleared after the
flush is successful.

Bug: 561994362
Fixed: 561994362
Change-Id: I8dbe91d8f6481af4542ff8f4023811efa6966f87
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8449772
Commit-Queue: Michael Ludwig <michaelludwig@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Kyle Charbonneau <kylechar@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1703817}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
M150 has no deferred should_clear_shared_image_ path in RasterDecoderImpl and SharedContextState::FlushWriteAccess() returns void, so the fix was ported by: adding should_clear_shared_image_ and marking the SharedImage cleared in DoEndRasterCHROMIUM() only when FlushWriteAccess() reports success; making FlushWriteAccess() return bool (Graphite: FlushGraphiteRecorder() result); removing the early representation->SetCleared() in WebGPUDecoderImpl::ClearSharedImageWithSkia() (upstream already only marks cleared after the submit) and returning the flush result from UploadContentsToSkia() as upstream does.

